<title>ITALY: Italy's Bologna sees Sept CPI at 4.2 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italy's Bologna sees Sept CPI at 4.2 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BOLOGNA, Italy 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Bologna said its September consumer price index stood at 1.0 percent month-on-month and 4.2 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In August, Bologna's inflation rate was flat and 3.5 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Bologna is one of 10 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Monday and Tuesday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 7.62 percent on the national index. The 10 sample cities have a combined weighting of 69.67 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to August 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     1.0   (0.0)     4.2  (3.5)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.1  (-0.4)     3.4  (3.7)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.1   (0.0)     3.0  (2.9)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.8   (0.3)     6.5  (5.8)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.1   (0.1)     3.1  (3.1)</p>
<p>    Health services		  -0.2   (0.1)     4.0  (4.6)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.0   (0.3)     4.5  (4.6)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     7.9   (0.0)    10.5  (3.9)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0  (-0.3)     1.4  (2.7)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.1   (0.0)     2.7  (2.8)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	-0.1   (0.1)     1.4  (1.6)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom ++392 66129526</p>
